I think since it changes the state of the game, it should use up some
game time. But maybe I'm wrong about that. What else can you do to
change the game state without any time elapsing?

The unpatched code is inconsistent about this. If an item vanishes and
you press ESC at the "Do what? (oib)" prompt, then no time passes. But
if you make it past that menu a turn will elapse whether you move any
items or not.

By setting used=1 at line 2123 of pickup.c, I think the Dev Tem
intended for this to use a turn. The bug, I think, is returning 0 at
line 2160 instead of used, as is returned everywhere else in
use_container().



